{"availability":"available","full":"CESNET/ndk-fpga","name":"ndk-fpga","description":"Network Development Kit (NDK) for FPGA cards with example application","category":"Developer tools","language":"VHDL","stars":99,"forks":17,"created":"2022-04-13T12:01:22Z","updated":"2026-10-08T13:37:44Z","license":"BSD-3-Clause","branch":"devel","homepage":"https://www.liberouter.org/ndk/","topics":["ethernet","fpga","liberouter","network-development-kit","vhdl"],"demo":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10035175","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:20:51.317Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:20:51.317Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:20:51.317Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:09.392Z","stars":99,"forks":17},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:12:12.301Z","stars":99,"forks":17},{"at":"2026-10-06T17:12:00.783Z","stars":99,"forks":17},{"at":"2026-10-07T23:31:47.646Z","stars":98,"forks":17},{"at":"2026-10-10T03:20:51.317Z","stars":99,"forks":17}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This repository contains FPGA part of the Network Development Kit (NDK) for FPGA acceleration cards. The NDK allows users to quickly and easily develop FPGA-accelerated network applications. The NDK is optimized for high throughput and scalability: it scales from 10G to 400G Ethernet, depending on the target card (see the table below). The NDK-based Minimal (reference) application is also included in this (NDK-FPGA) repository.","The NDK-based Minimal application is a simple example of how to build an FPGA application using the NDK. It can also be a starting point for your NDK-based application. The NDK-based Minimal application does not process network packets in any way; it only sends and receives them. If the DMA IP is enabled, then it forwards the network packets to the computer memory. You can find more detailed information in the NDK-FPGA documentation (devel branch) here.","Please note that some integrated IP (e.g. DMA Medusa IP) are not part of the open-source NDK-FPGA. These IPs can only be obtained through our partners, see the section Partners."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CESNET/ndk-fpga/blob/devel/README.md","fingerprint":"b6ed2ce29866641c3325ee59efdc26105ee604a1f82a99e570bc6de8159ab020","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:26:41.136Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:47.847Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T11:01:46Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:47.646Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This repository contains FPGA part of the Network Development Kit (NDK) for FPGA acceleration cards. The NDK allows users to quickly and easily develop FPGA-accelerated network applications. The NDK is optimized for high throughput and scalability: it scales from 10G to 400G Ethernet, depending on the target card (see the table below). The NDK-based Minimal (reference) application is also included in this (NDK-FPGA) repository.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CESNET/ndk-fpga/blob/devel/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"b6ed2ce29866641c3325ee59efdc26105ee604a1f82a99e570bc6de8159ab020","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CESNET/ndk-fpga/blob/devel/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:47.847Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CESNET/ndk-fpga/blob/devel/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:47.848Z","hash":"b6ed2ce29866641c3325ee59efdc26105ee604a1f82a99e570bc6de8159ab020","originalBytes":11717,"storedBytes":11717,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["x16","fpga","pro","prime","quartus","cards","build","documentation","comp","repository","card","ndk","partners","silicom","license","ndk-fpga","vivado","application","files","gen3","minimal","see","available","dma","firmware","branch","devel","git","license.","located","network","release","subject","their","xilinx","cabal","clone","ctrls","gen5","generated","github","how","intel","issues","n6010","ndk-based","pcie","please","src","support","were","add